        {
          "type": "kotak",
          "title": "Two ways to ask someone's name",
          "items": [
            "**מָה שִׁמְךָ?** *(mah shimkha?)* — formal, used on forms and in interviews. Literally \"what your-name?\".",
            "**אֵיךְ קוֹרְאִים לְךָ?** *(eikh kor'im lekha?)* — everyday, far more common. Literally \"how do they call to-you?\". The answer: **קוֹרְאִים לִי בּוּדִי** — \"they call me Budi\".",
            "The second form sounds odd when translated, but it's the one you'll hear nine times out of ten."
          ]
        }
